>only in si'o/du'u to see the contrast.

I would not use "du'u" in a bridi based on "senva".  We don't dream about
the facts of a matter - rather we free-associate around ideas.  If your
thinking is logical, and the truth/reality of each bridi is important, then
"du'u" is the word of cjhoice.  When you think about something, and the
importance is the concept, and not whether it is, or even could be, true
or real, then "si'o" is the preferred word.  Certainly unattainable ideals
are better marked with "si'o", and fantasy and science fiction would have to
be careful in choosing between the words - the distinction would change the
interpretation of the story considerably from a "what if this were true" to a
more fanciful or philosophical intent.

